[interviewer · CLARIFY · 1:33] Okay. Before I give you data, you've split this into revenue, costs, and mix. Hold that request; I'll come back to it shortly. Is that MECE, and which branch would you prioritize first, and why?

[candidate · 3:02] I think it's close to MECE, though mix isn't fully clean — it's really a driver that shows up inside both revenue and cost, not a separate bucket. I'd fold it under revenue as price-per-unit times volume, and keep costs separate as fixed versus variable. That's cleaner.

I'd prioritize costs first. Revenue grew 15%, so demand isn't the obvious problem, and a drop from 24% to 6% is 18 points of margin — that's huge. If revenue were flat and costs were flat, margin wouldn't move at all. So something on the cost side is scaling faster than revenue, or a fixed-cost block got added. I'd start by seeing which cost line grew fastest relative to revenue, then drill into that one.
